From 33cf46fbe02052c0f67fdb1ffbf22919c3fb1bf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:06:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(log): library and UI diagnostics become tracing
 events

The last slice of #163. The remaining eprintln! refusals and fallbacks in
camcraft-cl, -geometry, -motion, -sim and -tools are tracing events (warn;
the opt-in projection profile at info), and each standalone bin installs a
stderr subscriber with the app's CAMCRAFT_LOG / RUST_LOG rule so they still
reach its terminal. The ui diag seam emits tracing events natively, and the
native window, GPU bring-up, quit hook, frame watch and headless proof
speak through it; only test-only code still prints directly.

tracing and tracing-subscriber were already workspace dependencies; no new
crate and no camcraft-* edge.

Pinned by cl refusal_log::a_refused_axis_or_angle_is_a_warning_under_the_cl_target
and ui diag::tests::diag_lines_are_tracing_events_at_their_level.

Fixes #163

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
